BlueprintViewModel.rml<pre><code>&lt;viewmodel name="counter" class="/ArcRmlUISamples/UI/Rml/BlueprintViewModel/BP_SampleVM.BP_SampleVM_C" create="true"/&gt;
</code></pre> <p>A Blueprint view model is named by its generated class: the asset path, a dot, and the asset name followed by <code>_C</code>. <code>create="true"</code> makes a new instance when the document opens. The rest of the document reads the fields and calls the function like any other view model:</p> BlueprintViewModel.rml<pre><code>&lt;body data-model="counter"&gt;
    &lt;div class="bv-panel"&gt;
        &lt;h1 class="bv-title"&gt;{{ Title }}&lt;/h1&gt;
        &lt;p id="bv-count"&gt;Count: {{ Count }}&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;Step: {{ Step }}&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;div class="bv-buttons"&gt;
            &lt;button id="bv-increment" class="bv-button" data-event-click="call('', 'Increment')"&gt;Add step&lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;button class="bv-button" data-action="close"&gt;Close&lt;/button&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
</code></pre> <p><code>call('', 'Increment')</code> calls <code>Increment</code> on the model of the element's <code>data-model</code>; "Add step" adds <code>Step</code> to <code>Count</code>. <code>data-action="close"</code> closes the document.</p>

Card.rml<pre><code>&lt;component&gt;
    &lt;prop name="title" default="Card"/&gt;
    &lt;prop name="accentColor" default="#3399ff"/&gt;
    &lt;div class="cp-card"&gt;
        &lt;div class="cp-card-head" data-style-background-color="$accentColor"&gt;{{ $title }}&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div class="cp-card-body"&gt;&lt;slot/&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div class="cp-card-foot"&gt;&lt;slot name="footer"/&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/component&gt;
</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>&lt;prop name="title" default="Card"/&gt;</code> declares a prop and its default. A prop with no default and no value is empty text.</li> <li>The body reads a prop as <code>$title</code>: in an expression, as in <code>data-style-background-color="$accentColor"</code>, and inside   <code>{{ }}</code>, as in <code>{{ $title }}</code>.</li> <li><code>&lt;slot/&gt;</code> receives the children of the import. <code>&lt;slot name="footer"/&gt;</code> receives only the direct children that carry   <code>slot="footer"</code>.</li> </ul> <p>Where a component's styles go</p> <p>A component file holds markup only. Put its styles in the style sheet of the importing document (<code>Component.rcss</code> here), or in an <code>.rcss</code> file with the component's name next to it (<code>Card.rcss</code>), which the compile links into every document that imports the component.</p> <p>The sample takes the first way:</p> Component.rcss<pre><code>.cp-card {
    margin: 8px 0;
    background-color: #303846;
    border-radius: 4px;
}

.cp-card-head {
    padding: 6px 12px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: #101418;
}

.cp-card-body {
    padding: 8px 12px;
}

.cp-card-foot {
    padding: 4px 12px 8px;
}
</code></pre>

Component.rml<pre><code>&lt;dc-import name="/ArcRmlUISamples/UI/Rml/Component/Card" title="Static title" accent-color="#ff9933"&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;The default slot: any children.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p slot="footer"&gt;The footer slot.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/dc-import&gt;
&lt;dc-import name="/ArcRmlUISamples/UI/Rml/Component/Card" title="{{ Title }}"&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Pressed {{ Count }} times.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;button id="cp-press" slot="footer" class="cp-button" data-event-click="call('', 'Increment')"&gt;Press&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/dc-import&gt;
</code></pre>

EditorPreview.rml<pre><code>&lt;viewmodel name="player" preview="Preview/EditorPreview.json"/&gt;
</code></pre> <p>The path is relative to the document. A preview declaration takes no <code>class</code>, no source attribute (<code>create</code>, <code>context</code>, <code>resolver</code>, <code>manual</code> or <code>path</code>), no <code>settable</code> and no <code>on-close</code>.</p> Preview/EditorPreview.json<pre><code>{
    "Name": "Aldric",
    "Level": 7,
    "Health": 0.8,
    "Accent": { "$colour": "#3399ffff" },
    "bLowHealth": false,
    "Items": ["Stone axe", "Oak staff", "Iron shield"],
    "$variants": {
        "LowHealth": {
            "Health": 0.15,
            "Accent": { "$colour": "#e04040ff" },
            "bLowHealth": true,
            "Items": ["Stone axe"]
        }
    }
}
</code></pre> <ul> <li>The root is an object; each top-level key is a field of the model. Values are booleans, integers, numbers,   strings, arrays and objects. <code>null</code> is an error.</li> <li>A colour is <code>{ "$colour": "#rrggbbaa" }</code>, and <code>$colour</code> is the object's only member.</li> <li><code>$variants</code> is an object of named variants. A variant lists the fields it overrides; every other field keeps its   base value. An overridden field is replaced as a whole, so <code>Items</code> in <code>LowHealth</code> is the complete list. A variant   can name only fields the base data has, else the file does not load and an error is logged.</li> </ul> <p>The document reads these fields like any other model's: <code>{{ Name }}</code>, <code>data-if="bLowHealth"</code>, <code>data-for="item : Items"</code>.</p>

FormControls.rml<pre><code>&lt;input id="fc-subtitles" type="checkbox" autofocus=""
    data-checked="bSubtitles"
    data-event-change="call('', 'SetSubtitles', ev.checked)"/&gt;
&lt;label for="fc-subtitles"&gt;Subtitles&lt;/label&gt;
</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>data-checked</code> with a bool checks the box when the bool is true.</li> <li>A toggle by click, Space, Enter, gamepad accept or a click on its <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> fires <code>input</code>, then <code>change</code>. <code>ev.checked</code>   is the box's state after the toggle.</li> <li><code>ev.value</code> of a checkbox or radio is its <code>value</code> attribute (<code>on</code> without one), checked or not. Use <code>ev.checked</code> for the state.</li> </ul> <p>Bind a checkbox with <code>data-checked</code></p> <p><code>data-attr-checked="Flag"</code> writes the bool as text, so a false value sets <code>checked="0"</code>. Any <code>checked</code> attribute checks the control, so the box stays checked. <code>data-checked="Flag"</code> (a bool, or a string equal to the control's <code>value</code>) and <code>data-attrif-checked="Flag"</code> (the attribute is set when true and removed when false) check and uncheck correctly.</p>

FormControls.rml<pre><code>&lt;select id="fc-quality" data-attr-value="Quality" data-event-change="call('', 'SetQuality', ev.value)"&gt;
    &lt;option value="low"&gt;Low&lt;/option&gt;
    &lt;option value="medium"&gt;Medium&lt;/option&gt;
    &lt;option value="high"&gt;High&lt;/option&gt;
&lt;/select&gt;
</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>data-attr-value</code> selects the option whose <code>value</code> matches. <code>input</code> and <code>change</code> fire when a pick changes the value.</li> <li>On a closed select Enter, Space or gamepad accept open the list with the selected option highlighted. Up and Down move   the highlight, Home and End jump to the first and last option, and Enter, Space or gamepad accept pick it. A mouse click   on an option picks it.</li> <li>Esc or gamepad back close the open list and keep the value; the Back stops there and does not close the screen. On a   closed select Back works as usual.</li> <li>Up and Down on a closed select move focus; they do not change the value.</li> </ul>

Images.rml<pre><code>&lt;img class="im-box" src="Images/Picture.png" width="64" height="64"/&gt;
&lt;img class="im-box" src="Images/Sprites.png" rect="32 0 32 32" width="64" height="64"/&gt;
</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>src</code> is a <code>png</code> or <code>svg</code> file. A path that starts with <code>/</code> is a package path, any other path is relative to the   document (Coming from HTML and CSS).</li> <li><code>rect="x y w h"</code> draws that part of the file, in the file's pixels. Any other count of numbers logs a warning and the   whole file is drawn.</li> <li>Give every image a <code>width</code> and a <code>height</code>, or the layout jumps when the file loads: without both, the image is 0 by 0 until the   file is decoded, and the layout runs again.</li> </ul>

Images.rcss<pre><code>@spritesheet im-sprites {
    src: Images/Sprites.png;
    im-circle: 0px 0px 32px 32px;
    im-square: 32px 0px 32px 32px;
    im-diamond: 0px 32px 32px 32px;
    im-cross: 32px 32px 32px 32px;
}
</code></pre> Images.rml<pre><code>&lt;img class="im-sprite" sprite="im-circle"/&gt;
</code></pre> <p><code>@spritesheet</code> names the file, then each sprite as <code>name: x y w h</code>. <code>sprite</code> wins over <code>src</code> and <code>rect</code>.</p> <p>RmlUi only</p> <p><code>@spritesheet</code> and <code>sprite</code> have no counterpart in a browser. A sprite name that the document's style sheets do not declare draws nothing and logs <code>Could not find sprite</code>.</p>

Images.rml<pre><code>&lt;svg class="im-box" src="Images/Star.svg" width="64" height="64"/&gt;
&lt;svg class="im-inline im-inline-blue" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="64" height="64"&gt;&lt;path d="M12 2 L22 21 L2 21 Z" fill="currentColor"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>&lt;svg src="..."&gt;</code> draws an SVG file, sharp at any size.</li> <li>An <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code> without <code>src</code> draws its own content.</li> <li><code>currentColor</code> takes the element's CSS <code>color</code>, so one shape serves every colour: <code>.im-inline-blue</code> sets <code>color: #3a86ff</code>   and <code>.im-inline-green</code> sets <code>color: #3ccf6e</code>. This applies when the SVG text contains <code>currentColor</code> (case-sensitive) and   the <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code> has no <code>color</code> attribute.</li> </ul>

Images.rml<pre><code>&lt;svg id="im-bound-icon" class="im-box" data-attr-src="Icon" width="64" height="64"/&gt;
&lt;img id="im-bound-picture" class="im-box" data-attr-src="Picture" width="64" height="64"/&gt;
</code></pre> Images/ArcRmlSamplesImages.h<pre><code>UPROPERTY(BlueprintReadOnly, FieldNotify, Category = "Samples")
FArcRmlImageRef Icon;

UPROPERTY(BlueprintReadOnly, FieldNotify, Category = "Samples")
TSoftObjectPtr&lt;UTexture2D&gt; Picture;
</code></pre> Field type <code>src</code> becomes <code>FArcRmlImageRef</code> Its <code>Path</code>, the package path of an image file. The property editor's picker lists <code>.svg</code> files. <code>TSoftObjectPtr</code>, <code>FSoftObjectPath</code>, <code>UTexture*</code> <code>asset:&lt;path&gt;</code>; empty when nothing is set. <code>FString</code> The text as it is. <p>The sample's <code>Swap</code> function sets both fields, and the document follows the change (Data binding). The four values (<code>FirstIcon</code>, <code>SecondIcon</code>, <code>FirstPicture</code>, <code>SecondPicture</code>) are defaults of a Blueprint subclass of the view model, <code>BP_ImagesVM</code>, which the document names in its head. Set the image paths in a Blueprint subclass of your own view model the same way, and no path is written in C++.</p> <p>The validator checks a literal <code>src</code>, not a <code>data-attr-src</code> (Validation); a bound image that is not found is reported only at run time.</p>

GamepadMenu.rml<pre><code>&lt;meta name="input-mode" content="menu"/&gt;
&lt;meta name="input-mapping" content="/ArcRmlUISamples/UI/Rml/GamepadMenu/IMC_Sample_GamepadMenu"/&gt;
</code></pre> GamepadMenu.rml<pre><code>&lt;button id="gm-play" class="gm-button" autofocus="" data-event-click="call('', 'Choose', 'Play')"&gt;Play&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;button id="gm-options" class="gm-button" data-event-click="call('', 'Choose', 'Options')"&gt;Options&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;button id="gm-credits" class="gm-button" data-event-click="call('', 'Choose', 'Credits')"&gt;Credits&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;p class="gm-last"&gt;Last choice: {{ LastChoice }}&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="gm-info" data-if="bInfoShown"&gt;Arrows or the D-pad move the focus, {{ ArcKeys.confirm }} presses the focused button, {{ ArcKeys.back }} closes the menu.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="gm-prompts"&gt;
    &lt;span class="gm-prompt"&gt;{{ ArcKeys.confirm }} Select&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span id="gm-info" class="gm-prompt" data-hotkey="IA_Sample_MenuInfo" data-event-click="call('', 'ToggleInfo')"&gt;{{ ArcKeys.IA_Sample_MenuInfo }} Info&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="gm-prompt"&gt;{{ ArcKeys.back }} Close&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>input-mode</code> <code>menu</code>: the document takes keyboard, gamepad and mouse input while it is open.</li> <li>Arrows and the D-pad move the focus between the buttons. A <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> is a form control, so it takes focus and is a   navigation stop by default; <code>autofocus</code> on "Play" is where the focus starts. A <code>div</code> or <code>span</code> needs   <code>tab-index: auto; nav: auto</code> to become one.</li> <li>Confirm is always Enter, Space or gamepad accept (the gamepad's accept button, A in the samples) and presses the focused button. The CommonUI   click action only supplies its key label, <code>{{ ArcKeys.confirm }}</code>.</li> <li>Back is the back action of the project's CommonUI input data: Esc or gamepad back (B in the samples). A Back that no <code>data-event-back</code> handler stops closes   the document.</li> <li><code>{{ ArcKeys.confirm }}</code> and <code>{{ ArcKeys.back }}</code> show the keys of Confirm and Back for the current input device.</li> </ul> <p>The code above is an excerpt: the screen also declares its view model in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> and binds it with <code>data-model</code> on <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>.</p>

Menu.rml<pre><code>&lt;button id="ka-preload" class="ka-button" autofocus="" data-event-click="call('', 'Preload')"&gt;Preload&lt;/button&gt;
</code></pre> KeepAlive/ArcRmlSamplesKeepAlive.cpp<pre><code>void UArcRmlSamplesKeepAliveMenuViewModel::Preload(UObject* WorldContextObject)
{
    if (UArcRmlViewportSubsystem* Viewport = ArcRmlSamplesKeepAlive::GetViewport(WorldContextObject))
    {
        Viewport-&gt;PreloadDocument(ArcRmlSamplesKeepAlive::Preloaded);
    }
}
</code></pre> <p>This is an excerpt of the sample: <code>GetViewport</code> returns the local player's <code>UArcRmlViewportSubsystem</code> for the player controller, and <code>Preloaded</code> is the sample's <code>FArcRmlDocumentRef</code> for <code>Preloaded.rml</code>.</p> <p><code>PreloadDocument</code> (C++ and Blueprint) loads the document, lays it out and parks it without showing it, and remembers that its path is preloaded. <code>Preloaded.rml</code> has no <code>keep-alive</code> <code>&lt;meta&gt;</code>, yet the next open shows it at once.</p> <ul> <li>A preloaded document parks on every close, as a <code>keep-alive</code> one does, so its second open is as fast as its first.</li> <li>The preload starts once the local player controller exists, and its pawn when the game mode has a default pawn. It does not   start in a frame that opened a document. One preload runs at a time, the rest wait in the queue.</li> <li>A document that is already open or parked is not loaded again; asking twice for one path does nothing.</li> <li>An open that arrives while the preload still loads takes it over and shows it as soon as it is loaded. An open before the   preload started opens the document like any other and drops the queued preload.</li> <li>Opened before the first <code>PreloadDocument</code>, a document opens and closes like any screen.</li> </ul>

KeepAlive/ArcRmlSamplesKeepAlive.cpp<pre><code>void UArcRmlSamplesKeepAliveMenuViewModel::DiscardBoth(UObject* WorldContextObject)
{
    if (UArcRmlViewportSubsystem* Viewport = ArcRmlSamplesKeepAlive::GetViewport(WorldContextObject))
    {
        Viewport-&gt;DiscardDocument(ArcRmlSamplesKeepAlive::Kept);
        Viewport-&gt;DiscardDocument(ArcRmlSamplesKeepAlive::Preloaded);
    }
}
</code></pre> <p><code>Kept</code> is the sample's <code>FArcRmlDocumentRef</code> for <code>Kept.rml</code>; <code>GetViewport</code> and <code>Preloaded</code> are as above.</p> <p><code>DiscardDocument(Document)</code> (C++ only) and the console command <code>ArcRml.Discard &lt;Path&gt;</code> destroy the parked view, so the next open loads the document again: <code>Kept</code> then starts at count 0 with an empty field. A parked document stays until a discard, a reload or the end of the player's world; there is no eviction.</p> <ul> <li>A discard also forgets that the path is preloaded. A preload that still loads is dropped, and an open screen that parks   only because it was preloaded is destroyed when it closes.</li> <li>A kept screen that is still closing when the discard comes is destroyed at once instead of parking.</li> <li>An open screen that is not preloaded, and a document that was never loaded, is left alone; the log says so.</li> </ul>

Localization/ArcRmlSamplesLocalization.cpp<pre><code>void UArcRmlSamplesLocalizationViewModel::SwitchCulture(const FString&amp; Name)
{
    if (!FInternationalization::Get().SetCurrentCulture(Name))
    {
        UE_LOGF(LogArcRmlSamples, Warning, "ArcRmlSamples: culture '%ls' does not exist in this build", *Name);
    }
}
</code></pre> <p><code>call('', 'SwitchCulture', 'pl')</code> calls it. ArcRmlUI translates every open document again in place; no document is reopened, so focus, scroll and the count stay. The engine console command <code>culture=pl</code> does the same. The sample's view model also listens to <code>FInternationalization::Get().OnCultureChanged()</code>, so the <code>{{ Culture }}</code> readout follows a change from anywhere.</p>

TextFields.rml<pre><code>&lt;input id="tf-input" class="tf-field" type="text" placeholder="Type a name"
    data-attr-value="Live"
    data-event-input="call('', 'SetLive', ev.value)"
    data-event-change="call('', 'Commit', ev.value)"/&gt;
&lt;textarea id="tf-notes" class="tf-field tf-notes" placeholder="Type some notes"
    data-attr-value="NotesLive"
    data-event-input="call('', 'SetNotesLive', ev.value)"
    data-event-change="call('', 'CommitNotes', ev.value)"&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;
</code></pre> TextFields/ArcRmlSamplesTextFields.cpp<pre><code>void UArcRmlSamplesTextFieldsViewModel::SetLive(const FString&amp; Value)
{
    UE_MVVM_SET_PROPERTY_VALUE(Live, Value);
}

void UArcRmlSamplesTextFieldsViewModel::Commit(const FString&amp; Value)
{
    UE_MVVM_SET_PROPERTY_VALUE(Committed, Value);
    UE_MVVM_SET_PROPERTY_VALUE(CommitCount, CommitCount + 1);
}
</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>input</code> fires for every edit (typing, delete, paste, cut), so <code>Live</code> follows the field. <code>change</code> fires when focus leaves   the field, or on Enter in the <code>&lt;input&gt;</code>, when the text differs from the one at focus or at the last <code>change</code>. Enter in   the <code>&lt;textarea&gt;</code> inserts a line break. Both events carry <code>ev.value</code>.</li> <li>Show the model's text with <code>data-attr-value</code>, as the sample does; <code>data-value</code> sets the same <code>value</code> attribute. Neither   writes back: a model field is read-only to the document (Limits), so <code>data-event-input</code> calls a function   that stores each edit.</li> <li>A value written through <code>data-attr-value</code> fires no event. On a focused field the write does not become the committed   value, so <code>change</code> still fires when the field is left; echoing the field's own text writes the same value and the   caret stays.</li> <li><code>placeholder="..."</code> is shown while the field is empty and styled with <code>::placeholder</code>.</li> </ul>

SaveLoad.rml<pre><code>&lt;rml&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;title&gt;ArcRmlUI Demo Save / Load&lt;/title&gt;
    &lt;meta name="layer" content="UI.Layer.Menu"/&gt;
    &lt;meta name="input-mode" content="menu"/&gt;
    &lt;meta name="hide-lower" content="true"/&gt;
    &lt;meta name="keep-alive" content="true"/&gt;
    &lt;meta name="input-mapping" content="/ArcRmlUIDemo/Demo/Input/IMC_ArcDemo_SaveLoad"/&gt;
    &lt;link type="text/rcss" href="/ArcRmlUIDemo/UI/Rml/Demo/tokens.rcss"/&gt;
    &lt;link type="text/rcss" href="/ArcRmlUIDemo/UI/Rml/Fonts/Fonts.rcss"/&gt;
    &lt;link type="text/rcss" href="GameUI.rcss"/&gt;
    &lt;link type="text/rcss" href="SaveLoad.rcss"/&gt;
    &lt;viewmodel name="ui"
        class="/ArcRmlUIDemo/Demo/ViewModels/BP_ArcRmlDemoUIVM.BP_ArcRmlDemoUIVM_C"
        context="VM_ArcRmlDemoUI"/&gt;
    &lt;viewmodel name="saveload"
        class="/ArcRmlUIDemo/Demo/ViewModels/BP_ArcRmlDemoSaveLoadVM.BP_ArcRmlDemoSaveLoadVM_C"
        resolver="/Script/ArcRmlUIDemo.ArcRmlDemoViewModelResolver"/&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>layer</code>, <code>input-mode</code> and <code>hide-lower</code>: a menu over the screen below it, which is hidden while this one is open   (Documents).</li> <li><code>keep-alive</code>: closing parks the document, so the next open keeps its state.</li> <li><code>input-mapping</code>: the screen's own actions; <code>IMC_ArcDemo_SaveLoad</code> maps <code>IA_ArcDemo_Delete</code> (Del, gamepad X)   and <code>IA_ArcDemo_DevBar</code> (F10), which shows or hides the demo's panel of screen buttons. Confirm and Back come from the project's CommonUI input   (Input and gamepad).</li> <li>The style sheets: the demo's tokens and fonts, <code>GameUI.rcss</code> shared by every demo screen, and the screen's own   <code>SaveLoad.rcss</code> (Styling).</li> </ul>
